A||||8||3400Fiero||seized rotors||||8||
Z||000000||3400Fiero||03-09-2001||07:10 PM||||I was planning to replace my front rotors with slotted ones from KVR performance, but I cannot get the old ones off!!  I am pretty sure the last time I did brakes the rotors slid off pretty easily, but this time they will not budge!!  <P>Any suggestions??  Help!!<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||8
Z||000001||JetroGT||03-09-2001||08:11 PM||||Use an air impact wrench. Rent one if you have to. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-09-2001||09:22 PM||||88s should slide off. You may have to remove a little metal clip on one of the studs if the rotor has never been off. Otherwise, it's probably just rusted on. Wire brush around the center hole where it slides on the hub. Spray WD-40 or penetrating rust stuff around the center piece and around the lug nut holes and other holes. Tap it with a hammer. If you get any movement just keep working it back and forth until it comes off.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||voyagerspe||03-10-2001||12:00 AM||||you probably realize this but incase you dont .  the rotors are part of the hub.  Tap off the center dust cap with a screwdriver and hammer, remove the cotter pin then unscrew the castle nut.  The entire unit will pull off.||||reg||1
Z||000004||voyagerspe||03-10-2001||12:02 AM||||by the way im refering to the front rotors on 84 to 87 fieros<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||3400Fiero||03-10-2001||09:41 AM||||Thanks, DRH.  I'm pretty sure they are rusted on.  I will have to try the wire brush and WD-40. (it is an 88)<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||14
Z||000006||MontanaFiero||03-10-2001||03:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by voyagerspe:<BR><B>you probably realize this but incase you dont .  the rotors are part of the hub.  Tap off the center dust cap with a screwdriver and hammer, remove the cotter pin then unscrew the castle nut.  The entire unit will pull off.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>3400Fiero has an '88. They pull off just like the rear rotors.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg">   <BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||03-10-2001||06:35 PM||||Careful use of a BFH.  They will come loose just tap around the perimeter.  Talk kindly to them.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TheFiero64||03-11-2001||01:44 PM||||My 88 did that. I had to remove the spindle and support the rotor in a vice. Then I put a socket in the center hub and hit it with a sledge hammer until the rotor came off.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
